 "summary": "The tensor-product weight theory has no counterpart in Mathlib (which has no weight-space additivity for group representations, and whose TensorProduct/Decomposition.lean only decomposes M \u2297 N along one factor) or elsewhere in TauCeti, and it reuses Submodule.map\u2082 distributivity, TensorProduct.map\u2082_mk_top_top_eq_top, rid, and the iSupIndep/IsInternal API rather than re-deriving them. The three prior duplication findings (bare stdRep instantiation, second public det-twist form, hand-rolled map\u2082-to-comap bridge) are all deleted at this head, and the rename leaves no alias.",
